    "body": "Problem:\r\nA mark created by `nvim_buf_set_extmark()` while an undo block is open\r\nnever comes back on redo.\r\n\r\nAnalysis:\r\nUndo deletes the text it covers and collapses the range; redo replays\r\nthe splices, which re-insert the text but cannot re-expand the mark.\r\n`extmark_set()` records a position only for a mark it moves, not for one\r\nit creates.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nRecord the created position for redo; undo leaves the mark to the splice\r\nreplay, since it did not exist before the edit. Each side of a paired\r\nmark gets its own entry. Redo also revives a mark that undo invalidated,\r\nelse its position returns but its highlight does not.\r\n\r\nfix #30331 cc @luukvbaal @bfredl \r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-08-15T14:13:33Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This has a performance cost. But even before this change, _undo_ (not redo)  starts to see scaling issues at extmarks >200k... (edit: fixed https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41331 )\r\n\r\nbefore:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\nn=20000 marks=20000 after=20000 set=36.3ms undo=18.1ms redo=0.9ms\r\n\r\n# undo cost starts to dominate at high N\r\n$ N=200000 build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\nn=200000 marks=200000 after=200000 set=376.6ms undo=817.3ms redo=9.4ms\r\n\r\n$ N=999999 build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\nn=999999 marks=999999 after=999999 set=2302.8ms undo=13947.2ms redo=52.5ms\r\n```\r\n\r\nafter:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n$ build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\nn=20000 marks=20000 after=20000 set=33.2ms undo=17.5ms redo=53.9ms\r\n\r\n$ N=200000 build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\nn=200000 marks=200000 after=200000 set=391.9ms undo=830.9ms redo=787.5ms\r\n\r\n$ N=999999 build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\nn=999999 marks=999999 after=999999 set=2330.3ms undo=14006.3ms redo=4712.7ms\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>benchmark script</summary>\r\n\r\n\r\n    -- Cost of redo when many extmarks are created inside one open undo block.\r\n    --\r\n    -- The marks must be created while the undo block from the preceding edit is still open\r\n    -- (b_u_synced == false), which is what this script's straight-line execution guarantees:\r\n    -- nothing here returns to the event loop, so nothing syncs the block.\r\n    --\r\n    --   build/bin/nvim --clean -l extmark_redo_bench.lua\r\n\r\n    local n = tonumber(os.getenv('N')) or 20000\r\n\r\n    vim.cmd('enew')\r\n    local ns = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('bench')\r\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, true, { ('x'):rep(200) })\r\n\r\n    -- Undo block is still open here.\r\n    local t0 = vim.uv.hrtime()\r\n    for i = 1, n do\r\n      vim.api.nvim_buf_set_extmark(0, ns, 0, i % 100, { end_col = (i % 100) + 1 })\r\n    end\r\n    local set_ms = (vim.uv.hrtime() - t0) / 1e6\r\n\r\n    local before = #vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(0, ns, 0, -1, {})\r\n\r\n    t0 = vim.uv.hrtime()\r\n    vim.cmd('normal! u')\r\n    local undo_ms = (vim.uv.hrtime() - t0) / 1e6\r\n\r\n    t0 = vim.uv.hrtime()\r\n    vim.cmd('normal! \\18') -- CTRL-R\r\n    local redo_ms = (vim.uv.hrtime() - t0) / 1e6\r\n\r\n    local after = #vim.api.nvim_buf_get_extmarks(0, ns, 0, -1, {})\r\n\r\n    print(('n=%d marks=%d after=%d set=%.1fms undo=%.1fms redo=%.1fms'):format(\r\n      n, before, after, set_ms, undo_ms, redo_ms))\r\n\r\n</details>",
            "created_at": "2026-08-15T13:41:31Z",
